== connection semantics ==
http11 default: close=False want100=False
http11 close: close=True want100=False
http10 keep-alive: close=False want100=False
http10 default: close=True want100=False
http10 close beats keep-alive: close=True want100=False
expect 100: close=False want100=True

== token list lookup ==
a in a,,b: True
b in a,,b: True
empty token in a,,b: False
empty token in empty value: False
empty token after trailing comma: False
gzip with trailing comma: True

== status reason phrases ==
100: "Continue"
200: "OK"
204: "No Content"
301: "Moved Permanently"
400: "Bad Request"
404: "Not Found"
418: ""
431: "Request Header Fields Too Large"
500: "Internal Server Error"
503: "Service Unavailable"
599: ""

== response head serialization ==
200 + two fields: HTTP/1.1 200 OK\r\nContent-Type: text/plain\r\nContent-Length: 5\r\n\r\n
404 + no fields: HTTP/1.1 404 Not Found\r\n\r\n
599 unregistered: HTTP/1.1 599 \r\n\r\n

== sans-IO bodies ==
empty body: Done trailers=0
from_binary round-trip: Ok "hello"
from_binary empty: Ok ""
collect past max: Err MessageTooLarge(3)
hand-written two-chunk body: Ok "abcd"
failing body propagates: Err UnexpectedEof
take_buffered empty: Empty
take_buffered whole: Whole "hello"
take_buffered streaming: Streaming first="ab" second="cd" rest="ef"
take_buffered of failing body: Err UnexpectedEof
collect after probe: Ok "hello"
probe of failing body: Err UnexpectedEof

== method dispatch via binary patterns ==
[Get, Post, Put, Delete, Patch, Head, Options, Other(BREW)]
